-- `l4 format` prints a mixfix call written between its arguments back in
-- source order: a binary call (Alice `knows` Bob) and a chain
-- (2 `scaled` 3 `shifted` 4). It used to print the head first
-- (`knows` Alice Bob) and the keywords of a chain twice (smucclaw/l4-ide#918).
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Alice, Bob

GIVEN a IS A Person
      b IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
a `knows` b MEANS a EQUALS b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
a `scaled` b `shifted` c MEANS a * b + c

GIVEN q IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
chk q MEANS q `knows` Bob

#EVAL Alice `knows` Bob
#EVAL 2 `scaled` 3 `shifted` 4
